# 5. Function with a conditional nested three levels deep
#    (bench/references.md §5). This one fits the Phase-1 surface directly.
#
#   λx:Num. if 0 < x then (if 10 < x then (if 100 < x then 3 else 2) else 1) else 0
#
# The only change from the reference is that `x > 0` is written `0 < x`:
# Phase 1's operator set is Add/Sub/Mul/Lt/Eq, with no `>`, so the operands
# are swapped. The nesting — the actual subject of this reference program —
# is reproduced exactly.

# λx:Num. ⦇⦈
construct-lam
move-parent
rename x0
set-ann Num
move-child 0

# if 0 < x then ⦇⦈ else ⦇⦈
construct-if
construct-binop lt
construct-num 0
move-next-sibling
construct-var x0
move-parent
move-next-sibling

# if 10 < x then ⦇⦈ else ⦇⦈
construct-if
construct-binop lt
construct-num 10
move-next-sibling
construct-var x0
move-parent
move-next-sibling

# if 100 < x then 3 else 2
construct-if
construct-binop lt
construct-num 100
move-next-sibling
construct-var x0
move-parent
move-next-sibling
construct-num 3
move-next-sibling
construct-num 2

# ... else 1
move-parent
move-next-sibling
construct-num 1

# ... else 0
move-parent
move-next-sibling
construct-num 0
